  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Wisconsin total $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Award volume is high: 48,063 awards have been made so far, with an average award size of $58.2K. Year over year obligations are down 55.3%. Historical context shows variability: FY21 obligations were $5.8B, FY22 were $5.2B, FY23 were $5.3B, FY24 were $8.9B, and FY25 were $6.3B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in the state with $2B in obligations, and OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. is the dominant vendor with $1.9B in obligations. Health-related industries and manufacturing sectors also lead obligations, with Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $1.8B and Truck Trailer Manufacturing at $324M. This snapshot covers partial fiscal-year totals and reports contract obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2026 compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 55.3% year over year. FY26 obligations are $2.8B versus $6.3B in FY25 and $8.9B in FY24. The drop concentrates on fewer large obligations compared with those prior fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and vendors in Wisconsin right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $2B in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $408M and the Department of Agriculture with $162M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor with $1.9B, followed by OSHKOSH DEFENSE LLC with $433M and AMTEC CORPORATION with $267M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Wisconsin?",
      "a": "Federal contract obligations to Wisconsin are $2.8B in FY2026 to date. That total comes from 48,063 awards with an average award size of $58.2K, and obligations are down 55.3% year over year. By comparison, prior fiscal years were $5.8B (FY21), $5.2B (FY22), $5.3B (FY23), $8.9B (FY24), and $6.3B (FY25)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Wisconsin?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs awards the most contracts in Wisconsin, with $2B in obligations. The next largest buyers are the Department of Defense with $408M and the Department of Agriculture with $162M, followed by the Department of Justice with $43.4M and the Department of Homeland Security with $29.2M."
    },
